{{!-- The full-width subscribe band the design puts at the end of a reading Surface.

	{{> "newsletter" anchor="end-newsletter"}}      the Post Surface's, which "Follow" links to
	{{> "newsletter" anchor="newsletter" pt="pt-16"}}   the homepage's
	{{> "newsletter" anchor="newsletter" pt="pt-20"}}   the Feed's, which the design sits lower

	anchor    the id, so a link on the same page can reach it
	pt        the section's top padding, which the design sets per Surface

Ghost's own signup, not a form the theme invents: `data-members-form` and `data-members-email`
are the whole contract, Portal binds the submit out of {{ghost_head}}, and the report comes
back as classes on the form element. The identical contract, and the same three CSS rules,
serve the footer's column — see partials/chrome/footer.hbs for what portal 2.71 actually adds.

The copy is the publication's, from two theme settings rather than from this file, because a
buyer changing the promise on their subscribe block should not have to edit a template. It
renders only where members exist. --}}
{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
	<section
		{{#if anchor}}id="{{anchor}}"{{/if}}
		aria-labelledby="newsletter-head"
		class="container {{#if pt}}{{pt}}{{else}}pt-18{{/if}}">
		<div
			class="border-accent-border bg-accent-soft grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr))] items-center gap-9 rounded-md border px-10 py-12">
			<div>
				<p class="text-accent-strong font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Newsletter"}}</p>

				<h2
					id="newsletter-head"
					class="font-display text-h2 tracking-heading mt-3.5 max-w-[24ch] leading-[1.15] font-medium text-balance">{{@custom.newsletter_heading}}</h2>

				<p class="text-small text-muted-on-soft mt-3.5 max-w-[52ch] leading-[1.6]">{{@custom.newsletter_text}}</p>
			</div>

			<form
				data-members-form="signup"
				class="flex flex-col gap-3">
				<label
					for="newsletter-email"
					class="font-ui text-[13px] font-semibold">{{t "Email address"}}</label>

				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
					<input
						id="newsletter-email"
						type="email"
						data-members-email
						required
						autocomplete="email"
						placeholder="{{t "you@publication.com"}}"
						class="border-accent-border bg-surface font-ui text-text min-w-0 flex-[1_1_220px] rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-[13px] text-[15px]">
					<button
						type="submit"
						class="btn btn-primary font-ui cursor-pointer rounded-sm px-6 py-[13px] text-[15px] font-semibold">{{t "Subscribe"}}</button>
				</div>

				<p
					data-members-error
					role="alert"
					class="font-ui text-danger text-xs"></p>
				<p
					role="status"
					class="font-ui text-muted-on-soft members-sent text-xs">{{t "Check your inbox for the link."}}</p>
				<p class="font-ui text-muted-on-soft text-xs">{{t "No spam. Unsubscribe anytime."}}</p>
			</form>
		</div>
	</section>
{{/if}}
